# Environment names only: intentionally no values.
# Copy only the entries required by the command you intend to run into a private .env.
# All entries are commented out: uncomment and populate selected entries.
# Blank optional variables can override code defaults or cause parsing errors; omit them instead.
# This is a command-specific inventory, not a universal list of required settings.
# Never commit a populated .env or put keys/tokens into this example.
# Source references identify where to check required/conditional behavior.
# Keeper runtime names and signer requirements are documented in keeper/.env.example.
# Select deployment-script entries here; do not enable every keeper/backend setting at once.

